														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3608235">
									

<p>I definitely wanted to hit that note, but I also wanted it to be ambiguous:</p>
<p>1. Was it really God or some other malevolent being wanting to use Ignatius for its purposes?</p>
<p>After all, Ignatius is a monk, so appearing to him as a version of an angry Judeo-Christian God is a logical approach to get him to do something.</p>
<p>2. Is it there to punish the Foundation? Future generations or humanity as a whole? Specific people who won't be able to stop themselves from using it? Something else?</p>
<p>Mostly I wanted to to try to get on paper the feeling &#8212; instilled in me through years of quasi-religious education &#8212; that all my problems in life, all my sense of unease, stems from some omnipotent quasi-omnipotent entity constantly raging because I'm not kissing its ass 24/7.</p>

							</div>

								
