														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3610084">
									

<p>At first I thought there was way too much addended material, but damn if it doesn’t come together. Part of me still feels like the utility of this to the Foundation would outweigh the risks. A sharper, saner mind than Braun’s could divise case by case expsure logistics to assess the viability of various experiments or missions (for example, if a team would all expected to be killed in a given experiment, hey, we’ve got a magic actuaty for that). I’m not saying the scp wouldn’t prove too unpredictable, but the Foundation usually learns those lessons the hard way.</p>
<p>On the other hand, this is brilliantly put together already, making the most of a simple idea, so maybe ‘leave the damn thing alone’ is good policy for both the object and the scp. +1</p>

							</div>

								
					
